  "rai:dataLimitations": [
    "This review release is limited to 53 completed benchmark entries that passed the current shared rulebook and review process. It does not cover the full broader corpus of 200+ datasets discussed in the paper.",
    "The release describes executable task interfaces and benchmark metadata, but it does not redistribute raw EEG recordings. Access to source data depends on the original repositories, licenses, and consent conditions.",
    "Task validity is bounded by the available public documentation, scan-derived evidence, and release-time kernel support. Some potentially useful tasks remain excluded or marked as non-releaseable if the evidence chain is incomplete.",
    "This resource is intended for benchmark construction, dataset-to-task mapping, and downstream model evaluation. It is not recommended for clinical decision making or for claims that go beyond the documented task interfaces and source-dataset scope."
  ],
  "rai:dataBiases": [
    "The benchmark inherits bias from the underlying public EEG datasets, including uneven coverage across subject populations, laboratories, recording devices, and acquisition protocols.",
    "Paradigm coverage is not uniform. Well-documented motor imagery, sleep, seizure, and related benchmark families are more represented than many low-resource or narrowly documented EEG settings.",
    "Some source datasets include demographic, clinical, or task-design skew that may affect downstream model behavior and generalization."
  ],
  "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "This review release contains derived benchmark documentation and task metadata, not repackaged raw EEG recordings. However, the benchmark is derived from human-subject EEG datasets that may involve sensitive biomedical or demographic information such as age, sex, diagnosis, sleep state, seizure status, and related metadata. Access to the underlying raw data remains governed by the original repositories and their terms.",
  "rai:dataUseCases": [
    "Cross-dataset EEG benchmark construction and comparison under explicit task interfaces.",
    "Evaluation of EEG foundation models and other downstream EEG learning systems on documented and executable tasks.",
    "Research on dataset-to-task mapping, benchmark documentation, review workflows, and auditable task operationalization.",
    "Educational and methodological inspection of how public EEG datasets can be converted into reusable benchmark tasks."
  ],
  "rai:dataSocialImpact": [
    "Positive impacts include improved transparency, reproducibility, and auditability in EEG benchmarking by reducing undocumented task engineering and making task assumptions explicit.",
    "Potential risks include overclaiming generalization from benchmark performance, propagating source-dataset imbalance, or applying released task interfaces outside the documented evidence scope.",
    "The community-review workflow and shared rulebook are intended to mitigate hallucinated task claims, undocumented label engineering, and inconsistent benchmark construction."
  ],
  "rai:hasSyntheticData": false,
  "rai:annotationsPerItem": "This benchmark is not a per-record human-label dataset. Review happens at the document and task-definition level. Each released entry was reviewed within the NeuroAudit workflow before inclusion in this release.",
  "rai:annotatorDemographics": [
    "Annotators and reviewers are project contributors performing EEG dataset documentation and benchmark review.",
    "Formal demographic metadata about reviewers were not collected for this release."
  ],
  "prov:wasDerivedFrom": [
